  "worked_solution": "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x-1)^{\u2032}=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{x}_{n}-1}{(\\frac{1}{{x}_{n}})} \\\\  & ={x}_{n}-({x}_{n}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{n}-{x}_{n}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{x}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =2{x}_{0}-{x}_{0}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{x}_{0} \\\\  & =2(1.5)-(1.5)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1.5) \\\\  & =2.391\\,802\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =2{x}_{1}-{x}_{1}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{x}_{1} \\\\  & =2(2.391\\,802\u2026)-(2.391\\,802\u2026)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(2.391\\,802\u2026) \\\\  & =2.697\\,840\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}\u22482.392$ and ${x}_{2}\u22482.698,$ rounded to three decimal places.",
